From 58d9f903c1bae6d9eb11a3148d518475f4481539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reuben olinsky <reubeno@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:19:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] FALLBACK: omit the positive OOM score check from Go test
 discovery

Downstream-only for Azure Linux. The containerized RPM %check environment
may give the test child an inherited OOM score adjustment with a protected
minimum above 123. If so, writing 123 is a decrease that the unprivileged
test process cannot make.

Omit only pkg/sys.TestSetPositiveOomScoreAdjustment so the rest of the
containerd tests can run.

---
 pkg/sys/oom_linux_test.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/sys/oom_linux_test.go b/pkg/sys/oom_linux_test.go
index 9266f65..1d0d984 100644
--- a/pkg/sys/oom_linux_test.go
+++ b/pkg/sys/oom_linux_test.go
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ import (
 	"github.com/stretchr/testify/require"
 )

-func TestSetPositiveOomScoreAdjustment(t *testing.T) {
+func testSetPositiveOomScoreAdjustment(t *testing.T) {
 	// Setting a *positive* OOM score adjust does not require privileged
 	_, adjustment, err := adjustOom(123)
 	assert.NoError(t, err)
